# Linux storage emulation

A virtual SD card in SPI mode and a virtual W25Q-family NOR flash on one SPI
bus, each keeping its contents in a file, behind the mm.mcu seam on the
storage-linux board -- storage-linux-x86_64 and storage-linux-aarch64, one
manifest per architecture -- as platforms/linux/epaper and platforms/linux/lcd
put virtual panels there. mm.sdcard and mm.spiflash
drive them exactly as they drive real chips, and the files are the bytes a
real card and chip would hold: an image made with mkfs.fat or littlefs-python
mounts here, and an image written here can be copied to a card with dd.

store holds the storage the chips sit on, in memory or in a file; sdcard and
spiflash are the chips, which know nothing of mm.mcu; bus is the mm.mcu
platform over both, registering nothing, so tests can use it; device is that
platform over files named by the device map, registered as mm.mcu; socket
publishes the card as mm.sdcard.socket.
